+# Veron: SPARSE bundling for WebCore's JS bindings. Every kernel OOM on an
+# 8 GiB build machine named a bundle of generated JS-DOM bindings (worst:
+# anon-rss 5.13 GiB at bundle 8, -O2) -- not because these bundles hold
+# more files, but because each generated JS*.cpp is individually enormous
+# and template-heavy. Bundling THOSE at 3 files per TU cuts the peak to
+# roughly the range ordinary bundles already occupy, while the other ~8000
+# translation units keep the upstream bundle size and upstream cost.
+# Scoped to WebCore so JavaScriptCore's many small JS*.cpp files are not
+# fragmented. This is the inverse of the script's dense-bundle feature,
+# which the CMake build never engages.
+VERON_SPARSE_BUNDLE_SIZE = 3
+
